──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
What this covers
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The Home Assistant Add-On wrapper for the BusMatic stack:
- Dockerfile, run.sh, prepare.sh, build.sh, build.yaml, config.yaml
- rootfs/ (slim lighttpd reverse-proxy config)
- rega_session_mock.py (JSON-RPC stub for aiohomematic)
- DOCS.md, README.md

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Third-party material fetched at build time (not part of this repository)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The Docker image produced by `build.sh` `apt install`s the `debmatic`
package from <https://apt.debmatic.de/debmatic stable main>.  That package
ships eQ-3 closed-source components (rfd, HMServer.jar, /firmware,
/opt/HmIP, etc.) which are NOT licensed under GPL-2.  Their distribution
is governed by alex-mathieu's debmatic packaging (GPL-2 wrapper) and
eQ-3's own redistribution terms applied via debmatic.

Consequence: source distribution of THIS repository is unrestricted
under GPL-2-or-later.  Distribution of the BUILT Docker image is NOT
permitted as a binary redistribution channel for the eQ-3 components.
End users build the image themselves from upstream debmatic.

bmcond (busmatic-concentrator), staged into the build context by
`prepare.sh`, has its own LICENSE and CREDITS — see the bmcond
sister-directory or its standalone repository.
